    "result_text": "The build is green. The audit log confirms the behavior: `AUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-LEV-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-07 membershipLevel=3`.\n\nHere's what I changed to implement the numeric `membershipLevel`:\n\n**New computation on creation** \u2014 `AssignMembershipLevel.java` (new function class): starts at 1, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (leaving 4 for tenure). Wired into the create pipeline in `owners.POST.yml` right after `countNamesakes` (so `namesakeCount` is already set) and before the audit/save steps.\n\n**Stored field** \u2014 added `membershipLevel` (`membership_level` column) to `Owner.java` plus getter/setter, and the column to all four DB schemas (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`). Also fixed the positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)` rows in `hsqldb/data.sql` to match the new column count.\n\n**Response change** \u2014 removed the derived `membershipTier` MapStruct mapping in `OwnerMapper.java` (the stored `membershipLevel` now auto-maps by name), and replaced the `membershipTier` schema in `openapi.yml` with a `membershipLevel` integer (1\u20133) property so the DTO regenerates with the new field.\n\n**Audit** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated` now records `membershipLevel=` instead of the old tier notion. Also dropped the now-stale `membershipTier`/GOLD sentence from `CountHousehold`'s javadoc.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` (unique owner with email \u2192 level 3) passes, and the full suite is green.",
